@@ -0,0 +1,20 @@
+# 0003: Holds are partial and never touch the ledger
+
+Status: accepted (2026-10-29)
+
+## Context
+
+Checkout would rather hold what it can than fail a whole cart. On-hand must stay a purely
+physical figure.
+
+## Decision
+
+- `reserve` holds `min(requested, available)` per line and leaves out lines that get 0.
+  It raises `InsufficientStock` only when no line can hold anything. Invalid input rejects
+  the whole request. `place_order` stays all or nothing.
+- Reserving, releasing, expiring and confirming never write to the ledger. Holds lower
+  `available` only, and on-hand moves only through receipt, adjustment and shipment.
+- `receive` and `adjust` are never blocked by holds. If a write-off leaves on-hand below what
+  is held, available is floored at 0 and existing reservations stay as they are.
+- Confirm turns the hold into a PLACED order's allocation without re-checking on-hand.
+  Any shortage shows up at `ship_order`, same as with orders today.
