+++ b/specs/stock-reservations.md
@@ -0,0 +1,114 @@
+# Stock reservations
+
+## What and why
+
+Checkout needs to hold stock for a cart before payment, then either confirm the
+hold into an order or release it. Holds nobody confirms lapse on their own after
+a while. The cart service and the payment service retry their calls, so
+`reserve` is made idempotent with a caller-supplied idempotency key, and
+`confirm_reservation` / `release_reservation` are safe to repeat.
+
+## Interface (fixed by the owner, verbatim)
+
+> Interface — hidden tests call exactly this; `InventoryService(repository, ledger, clock)` keeps working as is:
+> - `InventoryService.reserve(warehouse: str, items: dict[str, int], idempotency_key: str) -> Reservation`
+> - `InventoryService.confirm_reservation(reservation_id: str) -> Order`
+> - `InventoryService.release_reservation(reservation_id: str) -> Reservation`
+> - `InventoryService.get_reservation(reservation_id: str) -> Reservation`
+> - `InventoryService.available(sku, warehouse)` must take holds into account.
+> - `inventory.models`: dataclass `Reservation` with `reservation_id: str`, `warehouse: str`, `items: dict[str, int]` (units held per SKU), `status: ReservationStatus`, `expires_at: datetime`, `order_id: str | None`; enum `ReservationStatus` with members `ACTIVE`, `CONFIRMED`, `RELEASED`, `EXPIRED`.
+> - `inventory.errors`: new `ReservationNotFound`, `ReservationExpired`, `InvalidReservationState`, `IdempotencyConflict` (all subclass `InventoryError`); reuse the existing errors where they fit.
+> - Time comes only from the injected clock. There is no background job: expiry must take effect without anyone calling a sweep.
+
+Additions in this change:
+
+- `InventoryService(repository, ledger, clock, *, reservation_ttl=timedelta(minutes=20))`.
+- `InventoryService.held(sku, warehouse) -> int`: units in live (ACTIVE, not lapsed) holds.
+
+## Rules
+
+### Reserve
+- `expires_at = clock.now() + reservation_ttl`, and the default TTL is **20 minutes**.
+- Validation works like `place_order`: unknown warehouse → `UnknownWarehouse`, unknown
+  SKU → `UnknownSku`, a quantity that is zero, negative or not an int → `InvalidQuantity`, no
+  lines → `InvalidOrder`, and an empty idempotency key → `InvalidOrder`. A rejected request
+  holds nothing, not even its valid lines.
+- **Partial holds:** each line holds `min(requested, available now)`. A line that gets 0 is
+  left out of `items` entirely. If no line can hold anything, the call raises
+  `InsufficientStock` and creates nothing.
+- Reservation ids are sequential: `RES-0001`, `RES-0002`, …
+
+### Idempotency key
+- Keys are unique across the whole system (all warehouses) and are remembered forever.
+- Same key with the same request (same warehouse and the same *requested* items) returns
+  the original reservation in its current status. Nothing new is created and `expires_at`
+  never moves.
+- Same key with a different warehouse or different requested items → `IdempotencyConflict`,
+  even if the original reservation is finished.
+- A failed `reserve` leaves no trace: no key, no id consumed, no hold.
+
+### Expiry
+- Only ACTIVE holds expire. From `expires_at` on (that instant included) an ACTIVE hold
+  counts as EXPIRED. Nothing has to run a sweep for that to happen: the status is worked out
+  from the injected clock whenever the hold is read or used.
+
+### Confirm
+- ACTIVE and live → a PLACED order in the same warehouse with exactly the held units. The
+  reservation becomes CONFIRMED and gets `order_id` set. Available doesn't change, because
+  the hold becomes the order's allocation. Stock isn't re-checked against on-hand.
+- CONFIRMED → returns the same order and creates nothing, at any time, even after
+  `expires_at`.
+- EXPIRED (including one that has only just lapsed) → `ReservationExpired`.
+- RELEASED → `InvalidReservationState`.
+- Unknown id → `ReservationNotFound`.
+
+### Release
+- ACTIVE and live → RELEASED, and its units are available again.
+- RELEASED or EXPIRED → no-op that returns it unchanged.
+- CONFIRMED → `InvalidReservationState`. To give the stock back, cancel the order instead.
+- Unknown id → `ReservationNotFound`.
+
+### Availability
+- `available = on_hand − allocated(PLACED orders) − held(live holds)`, per SKU per
+  warehouse, never below 0. A hold in one warehouse doesn't touch any other warehouse.
+- `place_order` can only take available stock. Otherwise it raises `InsufficientStock`,
+  all or nothing as before.
+- Reserving, releasing, expiring and confirming never write to the ledger and never change
+  on-hand. `receive` and `adjust` are never blocked by holds. If a write-off leaves on-hand
+  below what's held, available shows 0 and the reservations stay as they are.
+
+## Acceptance criteria (each is a test in `tests/test_reservations.py`)
+
+- [ ] `reserve` returns an ACTIVE reservation with `expires_at = now + 20 min` and `order_id None`.
+- [ ] A hold lowers `available` and leaves `on_hand` and the ledger untouched.
+- [ ] Partial hold: a line is capped at what's available, and a line with 0 available is omitted.
+- [ ] No line can hold anything → `InsufficientStock`, and nothing is created.
+- [ ] An invalid line (unknown SKU, bad quantity) or an unknown warehouse → error, and nothing is held.
+- [ ] `place_order` can't take held stock.
+- [ ] Holds are per warehouse.
+- [ ] At `expires_at - 1µs` the hold is ACTIVE. At `expires_at` it's EXPIRED and its units are available again, with no sweep.
+- [ ] The TTL is configurable through `reservation_ttl`.
+- [ ] Same key and same request → the same reservation, nothing new, `expires_at` unchanged, even after it's released or expired.
+- [ ] Same key and same items in a different order → the same reservation.
+- [ ] Same key with different items or a different warehouse → `IdempotencyConflict`.
+- [ ] Idempotency compares the *requested* items, not the held ones.
+- [ ] A failed `reserve` doesn't burn the key or a reservation id.
+- [ ] Confirm → a PLACED order with the held units. Available is unchanged and on-hand is unchanged.
+- [ ] Confirm twice, including after `expires_at` → the same order, and only one order exists.
+- [ ] Confirm an expired hold (including one at exactly `expires_at`) → `ReservationExpired`.
+- [ ] Confirm a released hold → `InvalidReservationState`.
+- [ ] Release frees the units. Releasing again is a no-op.
+- [ ] Release an expired hold → returns it unchanged, status EXPIRED.
+- [ ] Release a confirmed hold → `InvalidReservationState`.
+- [ ] Unknown reservation id → `ReservationNotFound` on get, confirm and release.
+- [ ] A write-off below the held amount → available 0, and the reservation is unchanged.
+- [ ] Existing tests still pass, and `InventoryService(repo, ledger, clock)` still works.
+
+## Non-goals / scope limits
+
+- No changes to the stock report (`StockRow`). Its `available` column reflects holds
+  automatically through `service.available`.
+- No sweeper, no background job, no extending a hold.
+- `allocated()` keeps its meaning: units in PLACED orders only.
+- No re-checking of on-hand at confirm.
+- No new dependencies.
